What:		/sys/kernel/mm/execmem_confine/
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Present when executable allocations (module text, BPF, kprobes,
		ftrace) are confined to a fixed physical window
		(CONFIG_EXECMEM_CONFINE, for example an arm64 CTXR window).
		All files are read-only and hold a byte count:

		====================  ==========================================
		window_bytes          size of the window
		pool_bytes            part of the window executable allocations
		                      can use (the rest holds the kernel image
		                      and memory reserved before the window)
		free_bytes            part of pool_bytes not in use
		module_reserve_bytes  part of the pool BPF JIT images can't use,
		                      so that module text still loads when the
		                      rest is full
		====================  ==========================================
